videos.script:
Your SQL session starts in fifteen minutes. The phone buzzes, and the student puts the kettle down. {{buzz}}

That message took a long road. Your server handed it to Google or to Apple, who passed it to a service on the phone, which showed it, maybe without waking your app at all. {{path}} Along the way it needed an address, the device token, and that address changes. {{token}}

You will build the message for both services and measure it against the size they allow. {{payload}} Then you will work out the week's reminders on the phone itself, with no server, fifteen minutes before each session. {{local}}

A push is not guaranteed and not always on time. And it is the one way an app can tap someone on the shoulder. {{shoulder}} Spend it on reminders people asked for, or they will turn you off.
